  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-SIGN-UNSUPPORTED-NAME-GLYPH-001",
      "severity": "P2 provisional; an admitted operator name can trigger an unconditional missing-glyph assertion when its nearby shop lettering is painted",
      "classification": "new 95e producer-to-render source trace with independently inspected bundled font bytes; actual populated scene and runtime outcome remain unverified",
      "detail": "RenderedPersonalName permits any nonempty, trimmed name of at most 160 non-control characters. The single-character name Ж (U+0416) meets those source checks. ShopName::for_operator derives Ж’s Tavern for an inn, and ShopSign::for_establishment selects GrenzeGotisch by default. The bundled GrenzeGotisch and UnifrakturCook Unicode cmap subtables have no nonzero glyph mapping for U+0416, while their A and right-apostrophe entries are present. Locked ab_glyph/owned_ttf_parser/ttf-parser source turns a missing Unicode cmap mapping into GlyphId(0). SignTexture::paint calls line_width on the full sign text, and layout unconditionally asserts that each glyph ID is nonzero. Hence a call reaching layout for this valid name hits that assertion. Font table parsing was evidence inspection only; no Rust constructor, font painting, scene, client or runtime operation was executed.",
      "consumer_and_safeguards": "The tactical request captures the character display name for assigned resident operators; the dispatcher re-admits it as RenderedPersonalName and binds derived ShopName to the business. Scene establishment validation checks identity, use and matching derived name, not font coverage. The client constructs a sign when an establishment and compatible sign site are present; board-only presentation allocates no lettering texture. Its active-camera update requests SignDetail::Lettering within 48 m, at which point the selected material path calls SignTexture::paint. These are conditional source paths: a living assigned operator with this name, a successfully accepted scene and usable sign site, a nearby active camera, actual panic handling and player impact have not been observed.",
      "connected_scope": "Personal-name projection and tactical snapshot admission; business/scene brand derivation; sign text and glyph policy; bundled font coverage; lettering cache and client distance gating; error/fallback ownership and historical aliases.",
      "proposed_repair": "After audit completion and implementation authorization, make lettering safe for every supported admitted display name, for example by a deliberate glyph fallback/font-coverage strategy or an explicit recoverable rendering boundary, while retaining the player-facing name authority. Do not globally reject otherwise valid personal names merely to fit one font without an explicit product policy.",
      "later_acceptance": "When product validation is authorized, cover U+0416 and other admitted unsupported code points with both fonts, authored and captured operator identities, the board-only and nearby-lettering paths, appropriate fallback/diagnostic behavior, and ordinary German text and emblem layout.",
      "historical_related_candidates": [
        "SEGOVB-L13-SIGN-SITE-PHYSICAL-RETENTION"
      ],
      "relationship_qualification": "The recovered 059 record concerns sign site geometry and image-size admission, not this name/glyph first failure; both share the paint path but are not automatically aliases. A bounded 059 ledger/queue term search found no missing-glyph assertion record, not proof of global absence. No checkpoint 3821 recovery or historical unique count change is inferred.",
      "discovery": "partial; actual operator population and assignment, all supported names and fonts, scene/render execution, panic policy, full aliases and independent lenses remain open",
      "repair": "not started",
